So, the people who--

00:11:12.368 --> 00:11:14.082
- I bet ya they're gonna shake hands

00:11:14.082 --> 00:11:15.876
and then raise their, one of their legs.

00:11:15.876 --> 00:11:16.975
- There they go, they're doing that

00:11:16.975 --> 00:11:17.808
dumb pose again.

00:11:17.808 --> 00:11:18.641
So--
- And why?

00:11:18.641 --> 00:11:19.650
- That is part of it.

00:11:19.650 --> 00:11:23.090
I'm just saying that that is part of the--

00:11:23.090 --> 00:11:25.249
- It's one of the biggest
parts of the game.

00:11:25.249 --> 00:11:26.082
- System.

00:11:26.082 --> 00:11:28.308
- Before you even get into the party,

00:11:28.308 --> 00:11:30.500
you got to do this and, matter of fact,

00:11:30.500 --> 00:11:32.430
you could just stop there.

00:11:32.430 --> 00:11:36.330
Because it's such an
important part of the party,

00:11:36.330 --> 00:11:38.280
you could make an argument, and I think

00:11:38.280 --> 00:11:40.610
many celebrities do, in their own mind.

00:11:40.610 --> 00:11:42.730
They show up for the red carpet, and then

00:11:42.730 --> 00:11:44.566
they just leave and don't
even go to the party

00:11:44.566 --> 00:11:45.550
because they got their picture taken,

00:11:45.550 --> 00:11:48.280
proof that they were
there, because the game,

00:11:48.280 --> 00:11:50.867
or at least a big aspect of it, is--

00:11:52.890 --> 00:11:56.820
Looking like you belong
with the cool people.

00:11:56.820 --> 00:11:59.730
It's like, oh, this is a cool thing,

00:11:59.730 --> 00:12:01.830
and here's a picture of that person at it.

00:12:02.720 --> 00:12:04.040
That's it.

00:12:04.040 --> 00:12:06.810
I can prove I'm in the group.

00:12:06.810 --> 00:12:07.840
I'm in the group.

00:12:07.840 --> 00:12:08.998
- Yeah.

00:12:08.998 --> 00:12:10.775
- I got my picture in the same place

00:12:10.775 --> 00:12:12.580
that these other, like, Jeff Goldblum

00:12:12.580 --> 00:12:13.800
got his picture.

00:12:13.800 --> 00:12:14.633
- Right.

00:12:14.633 --> 00:12:17.676
- And then you go into
the party after that

00:12:17.676 --> 00:12:19.370
and you're like, okay
yeah, like 90% of this

00:12:19.370 --> 00:12:20.203
is done.

00:12:20.203 --> 00:12:21.300
It's like you, because
you got your picture,

00:12:21.300 --> 00:12:22.975
you got your credit.

00:12:22.975 --> 00:12:25.817
- And so, the way that we approach these

00:12:25.817 --> 00:12:28.170
parties though, and
this is what we're gonna

00:12:28.170 --> 00:12:30.700
get into, it's not the...

00:12:30.700 --> 00:12:32.280
Obviously we do the red carpet thing.

00:12:32.280 --> 00:12:33.456
We get the picture.

00:12:33.456 --> 00:12:37.160
So somebody who writes
something on the internet

00:12:37.160 --> 00:12:39.900
will associate us with
this particular event.

00:12:39.900 --> 00:12:43.310
But of course, we approach it, you know,

00:12:43.310 --> 00:12:47.340
yeah, okay, we may have a
show that's very popular,

00:12:47.340 --> 00:12:50.820
in certain circles, and
we may have some stuff

00:12:50.820 --> 00:12:52.807
to show and some stuff to be able to say,

00:12:52.807 --> 00:12:54.130
"hey, we should be here."

00:12:54.130 --> 00:12:55.875
I mean, we've created this and that.

00:12:55.875 --> 00:12:58.530
But what we're kind of,
the overarching thing

00:12:58.530 --> 00:12:59.900
that we're thinking, when we're there,

00:12:59.900 --> 00:13:02.453
is really the sort of,
the perspective of like,

00:13:03.720 --> 00:13:07.400
13 year old Rhett and Link, you know?

00:13:07.400 --> 00:13:08.438
- [Link] Yeah.

00:13:08.438 --> 00:13:10.341
- Buies Creek Elementary School.

00:13:10.341 --> 00:13:13.530
It's like, there's a lot
of famous people here,

00:13:13.530 --> 00:13:15.271
who do you want to talk to?

00:13:15.271 --> 00:13:17.230
(Rhett laughing)
You know, really.

00:13:17.230 --> 00:13:18.063
- Right.

00:13:18.063 --> 00:13:19.500
- Or, how good is the food?

00:13:19.500 --> 00:13:20.842
- Where?
- Where is the food?

00:13:20.842 --> 00:13:21.675
How much is it?

00:13:21.675 --> 00:13:23.380
How big are the plates?

00:13:23.380 --> 00:13:24.230
- Well, there's two things going.

00:13:24.230 --> 00:13:27.063
There's learning the
game which is, you know,

00:13:27.063 --> 00:13:30.500
it's a challenge, that,
in trying to figure out

00:13:30.500 --> 00:13:32.590
how this game is played and, you know,

00:13:32.590 --> 00:13:34.580
how do you get points, and how do you

00:13:34.580 --> 00:13:37.080
advance your strategy
and all those things,

00:13:37.080 --> 00:13:39.150
that's interesting.

00:13:39.150 --> 00:13:42.880
Observing it as an outsider,
is very entertaining,

00:13:42.880 --> 00:13:44.194
to us, I believe.

00:13:44.194 --> 00:13:45.027
- Oh yeah.

00:13:45.027 --> 00:13:47.834
- And hence why we're
happy to talk about it.

00:13:47.834 --> 00:13:48.667
- Right.

00:13:48.667 --> 00:13:50.596
- But then there's also an aspect of it

00:13:50.596 --> 00:13:53.580
that is, you know, then you're actually,

00:13:53.580 --> 00:13:55.910
you're trying to get to know people.

00:13:55.910 --> 00:13:58.572
There is another part of the game that is

00:13:58.572 --> 00:14:01.300
getting to know people that are successful

00:14:01.300 --> 00:14:04.810
at getting things done
and making connections.

00:14:04.810 --> 00:14:08.053
Because it is that, who
you know, and who you met,

00:14:08.053 --> 00:14:10.120
and when you met him, and
how was their breath cuz,

00:14:10.120 --> 00:14:11.550
do you like them?

00:14:11.550 --> 00:14:13.509
Do you want to keep working with them?

00:14:13.509 --> 00:14:14.342
- Or how is their breath huh?

00:14:14.342 --> 00:14:16.220
- You know, that type of
stuff, because they're

00:14:16.220 --> 00:14:17.390
just humans, too.

00:14:17.390 --> 00:14:19.693
So it's humans working with humans.

00:14:19.693 --> 00:14:20.720
So you got to work that part of it.

00:14:20.720 --> 00:14:23.230
But then the question in my mind,

00:14:23.230 --> 00:14:25.010
and this will become
painfully obvious once we

00:14:25.010 --> 00:14:29.390
get into what happened
is, man, is it worth it?

00:14:29.390 --> 00:14:32.978
It turns out there's
a lot of risk involved

00:14:32.978 --> 00:14:34.930
in trying to play this game.

00:14:34.930 --> 00:14:36.007
There's a risk of--

00:14:36.993 --> 00:14:39.000
- I think there's risk
when you play the game.

00:14:39.000 --> 00:14:41.920
- All types of emotional, if not--

00:14:41.920 --> 00:14:43.580
- Which is--

00:14:43.580 --> 00:14:47.040
- Physical injury, emotional injury,

00:14:47.040 --> 00:14:48.323
embarrassment.

00:14:49.230 --> 00:14:51.330
Man, it really does feel, a lot of times,

00:14:51.330 --> 00:14:53.950
like it's your first day in high school

00:14:53.950 --> 00:14:56.360
walking around the cafeteria
with your lunch tray

00:14:56.360 --> 00:14:59.180
trying to figure out who do you sit with

00:14:59.180 --> 00:15:01.150
or who do you sit next to
and is there gonna be an

00:15:01.150 --> 00:15:05.763
open seat at all or am
I gonna trip and fall?

00:15:06.870 --> 00:15:09.040
And boy the risk is real.

00:15:09.040 --> 00:15:12.300
I'll just leave it at that
for the moment, but um--

00:15:12.300 --> 00:15:13.927
- Yeah and hopefully--
- A little unpacking.

00:15:13.927 --> 00:15:16.153
- Entertaining to you.

00:15:16.153 --> 00:15:18.350
But before we get into
the stories, we do want to

00:15:18.350 --> 00:15:20.840
let you know that you can grab...

00:15:21.940 --> 00:15:22.920
A hat!

00:15:22.920 --> 00:15:26.260
We got, you know, they're calling these

00:15:26.260 --> 00:15:29.120
dad hats, it's what the youths are into

00:15:29.120 --> 00:15:30.930
these days.
- Mm-hmm.

00:15:30.930 --> 00:15:32.420
- We've got a tan one.

00:15:32.420 --> 00:15:35.430
We've got a black one with
a mythical logo on it,

00:15:35.430 --> 00:15:36.820
the Randler.

00:15:36.820 --> 00:15:37.653
- It's nice.

00:15:37.653 --> 00:15:40.780
- Link, the one that you have on has some,

00:15:40.780 --> 00:15:43.370
like actual metal buttons on the side.

00:15:43.370 --> 00:15:44.900
- This is nice workmanship.

00:15:44.900 --> 00:15:46.870
- There's leather straps in the back.

00:15:46.870 --> 00:15:48.940
- Yeah, so you can get that.

00:15:48.940 --> 00:15:53.803
- Also, we are selling,
at amazon.com/mythical,

00:15:53.803 --> 00:15:58.140
we are selling the
blu-ray, yes this is still

00:15:58.140 --> 00:15:59.900
a thing, this is still a technology.

00:15:59.900 --> 00:16:01.550
There are still blu-ray player--

00:16:01.550 --> 00:16:03.170
- I'm going to call
this a collector's item,

00:16:03.170 --> 00:16:05.184
The Tour Mythicality: Live in Los Angeles.

00:16:05.184 --> 00:16:08.810
- Yeah, so that was when we
recorded the entire tour.

00:16:08.810 --> 00:16:12.140
Obviously it's available,
you know, on other

00:16:12.140 --> 00:16:14.040
platforms like iTunes, but you can get

00:16:15.137 --> 00:16:17.120
the physical thing, the physicality of

00:16:17.120 --> 00:16:19.090
The Tour of Mythicality.

00:16:19.090 --> 00:16:19.931
- Yeah.

00:16:19.931 --> 00:16:21.250
- And there's a disc inside of that,

00:16:21.250 --> 00:16:23.309
for those of you who don't understand

00:16:23.309 --> 00:16:24.349
what blu-ray is.

00:16:24.349 --> 00:16:25.385
It's a disc.

00:16:25.385 --> 00:16:26.430
You take that round thing, you insert it,

00:16:26.430 --> 00:16:30.633
not into your mouth, but
into a blu-ray player.

00:16:30.633 --> 00:16:33.719
And then it's a video that will play.

00:16:33.719 --> 00:16:34.900
- It's just nice to have
even if you never watch.

00:16:34.900 --> 00:16:38.370
- There's like a menu, and you can click

00:16:38.370 --> 00:16:40.050
on different options.

00:16:40.050 --> 00:16:41.820
It's very advanced.

00:16:41.820 --> 00:16:45.470
Basically defines, you
know, our adolescent years.

00:16:45.470 --> 00:16:47.050
Or at least--

00:16:47.050 --> 00:16:48.880
- Amazon.com/mythical--

00:16:48.880 --> 00:16:49.713
- Teenagers.

00:16:49.713 --> 00:16:53.370
- And mythical.store, get it.

00:16:53.370 --> 00:16:57.990
- Okay, so do you want to
talk about the GQ party?

00:16:57.990 --> 00:16:59.650
- Yeah, let's talk about
them in chronological

00:16:59.650 --> 00:17:01.280
order because I think,
there's things that we

00:17:01.280 --> 00:17:03.740
learned that, then the
question with the Golden Globes

00:17:03.740 --> 00:17:06.710
party is where any of
those lessons then applied.

00:17:06.710 --> 00:17:08.220
- I think somewhere.

00:17:08.220 --> 00:17:11.190
- I think that's one
of the main questions.

00:17:11.190 --> 00:17:14.980
And plus I just want to get
this whole GQ experience.

00:17:14.980 --> 00:17:17.140
I just want to cleanse it from my system.

00:17:17.140 --> 00:17:20.230
But, so put it on the
internet, it's gonna hurt.

00:17:20.230 --> 00:17:24.030
It might hurt a little
bit, but at least it'll be

00:17:24.030 --> 00:17:26.722
out of me and on to you.

00:17:26.722 --> 00:17:27.555
(Link laughing)

00:17:27.555 --> 00:17:31.160
- Okay so I can talk a little
bit about the philosophy

00:17:31.160 --> 00:17:32.810
of how we operate at these parties.

00:17:32.810 --> 00:17:34.147
Okay, so.

00:17:34.147 --> 00:17:35.439
- Well, Stevie was with us.

00:17:35.439 --> 00:17:36.540
- So yeah, well, yeah, that's part of it.

00:17:36.540 --> 00:17:37.951
So--

00:17:37.951 --> 00:17:39.887
- That's the first, she was
with us for that one, anyway.

00:17:39.887 --> 00:17:44.380
- Stevie went with us to the
GQ party, which, you know,

00:17:44.380 --> 00:17:47.435
I think there's a different dynamic when

00:17:47.435 --> 00:17:50.340
it's just two guys
walking around the party

00:17:50.340 --> 00:17:54.006
like we had at the Golden Globes HBO party

00:17:54.006 --> 00:17:56.700
then when you've got,
sort of three people,

00:17:56.700 --> 00:17:58.870
two guys and a girl, cuz
now you kind of seem like,

00:17:58.870 --> 00:18:00.940
this is a group and at any time that you

00:18:00.940 --> 00:18:03.450
just begin talking to each
other, you just look like

00:18:03.450 --> 00:18:05.310
people who are a group of people talking.

00:18:05.310 --> 00:18:06.750
But two guys talking to each other--

00:18:06.750 --> 00:18:08.437
- Yeah, they came together.

00:18:08.437 --> 00:18:10.060
- Doesn't a constitute a group, really.

00:18:10.060 --> 00:18:11.199
- [Link] Right.

00:18:11.199 --> 00:18:12.713
- Especially when they both have on

00:18:12.713 --> 00:18:13.546
tuxes and look, obviously your friends

00:18:13.546 --> 00:18:15.228
in the way that we were
kind of in the (mumbles).

00:18:15.228 --> 00:18:16.061
- [Link] Yeah.

00:18:16.061 --> 00:18:18.048
They're not talking to anyone except who

00:18:18.048 --> 00:18:19.136
they came with.

00:18:19.136 --> 00:18:20.130
But with three, there's a question.

00:18:20.130 --> 00:18:21.567
- Right.

00:18:21.567 --> 00:18:22.400
- That's good.

00:18:22.400 --> 00:18:25.583
- And, you know, I'm
gonna, before we expose,

00:18:28.390 --> 00:18:31.600
Link, a little bit, I'm
going to build him up

00:18:31.600 --> 00:18:32.433
a little bit.

00:18:33.440 --> 00:18:36.530
Because Link, between the two of us,

00:18:36.530 --> 00:18:40.670
is the one who is more
fearless and just beginning

00:18:40.670 --> 00:18:41.820
to talk to somebody, right?

00:18:41.820 --> 00:18:44.090
He's always been the one that would go up

00:18:44.090 --> 00:18:46.159
to somebody, kind of
initiate a conversation.

00:18:46.159 --> 00:18:49.950
I'm very standoffish
in like, self-conscious

00:18:49.950 --> 00:18:52.390
and don't like to do that.

00:18:52.390 --> 00:18:55.210
I don't ever talk to
celebrities when I see 'em,

00:18:55.210 --> 00:18:56.900
even if I'm a fan.

00:18:56.900 --> 00:18:58.530
But Link is very comfortable with that.

00:18:58.530 --> 00:19:01.460
It leads to some great
opportunities and some

00:19:01.460 --> 00:19:03.416
great mishaps as you will see.

00:19:03.416 --> 00:19:04.560
- Well, it's, I mean, the whole point is

00:19:04.560 --> 00:19:06.650
to talk to people, to get to know people

00:19:06.650 --> 00:19:07.483
at a party.

00:19:07.483 --> 00:19:08.544
- No. No, wait, no, it's great.

00:19:08.544 --> 00:19:09.377
And so--

00:19:09.377 --> 00:19:11.030
- But it is very difficult
to talk to people.

00:19:11.030 --> 00:19:11.863
I mean--
- Yeah.

00:19:11.863 --> 00:19:13.730
- Again, it goes back to that whole like,

00:19:14.753 --> 00:19:16.995
you're in high school and you're like,

00:19:16.995 --> 00:19:18.303
you don't know anybody in the cafeteria.

00:19:19.356 --> 00:19:21.040
And you're like, to make
your way you got to start

00:19:21.040 --> 00:19:24.490
meeting people and there
is a pecking order.

00:19:24.490 --> 00:19:25.323
- Yeah, well--

00:19:25.323 --> 00:19:26.750
- It's like, no but, I
mean, who's gonna come up

00:19:26.750 --> 00:19:27.600
and talk to us?

00:19:27.600 --> 00:19:29.630
- Right, well, and to--

00:19:29.630 --> 00:19:30.689
- - There are exceptions.

00:19:30.689 --> 00:19:32.070
- Kind of contrast it, and so obviously

00:19:32.070 --> 00:19:34.648
it's one of those things
that like, this is like

00:19:34.648 --> 00:19:36.200
life advice, right?

00:19:36.200 --> 00:19:39.470
So, when you are with somebody who has

00:19:39.470 --> 00:19:41.430
a particular strength, just let them

00:19:41.430 --> 00:19:42.440
do that thing, right?

00:19:42.440 --> 00:19:44.866
Don't, I have absolutely,
I don't care at all

00:19:44.866 --> 00:19:47.736
that he's the one that ends...

00:19:47.736 --> 00:19:50.060
Like if Link and I are
helping someone move,

00:19:50.060 --> 00:19:52.430
for instance, well you
know what Links gonna do?

00:19:52.430 --> 00:19:55.710
He's gonna be the one that
is in the moving truck

00:19:55.710 --> 00:19:58.570
organizing and tetrasing the stuff into

00:19:58.570 --> 00:19:59.403
the moving truck.

00:19:59.403 --> 00:20:00.770
- Yeah and you're gonna be eating whatever

00:20:00.770 --> 00:20:02.170
food they provide.
- Right.

00:20:03.188 --> 00:20:04.365
Now, and I got a--

00:20:04.365 --> 00:20:05.780
- I've got a bad back, you know.

00:20:05.780 --> 00:20:08.110
- And so--
- Where your doughnuts?

00:20:08.110 --> 00:20:10.060
- Not only is he good at that but he likes

00:20:10.060 --> 00:20:11.280
to do that.

00:20:11.280 --> 00:20:13.390
Let someone use their gifts.

00:20:13.390 --> 00:20:16.540
So when we go to a party
together I'm like, all right.

00:20:16.540 --> 00:20:18.969
Like when I went to the Queer
Eye for the Straight Guy

00:20:18.969 --> 00:20:22.720
premiere party with my
wife, just the two of us.

00:20:22.720 --> 00:20:23.553
- Yeah.

00:20:23.553 --> 00:20:24.890
- She's a big fan of the show.

00:20:24.890 --> 00:20:28.390
I am, sort of, a
proximate fan of the show,

00:20:28.390 --> 00:20:29.490
through her.
- Mm-hm.

00:20:30.630 --> 00:20:32.050
- And have watched it
with her a few times.

00:20:32.050 --> 00:20:36.240
And we really wanted to
talk to some of the cast,

00:20:36.240 --> 00:20:37.807
but she's just--

00:20:37.807 --> 00:20:39.973
- You wanted to lock a queer eye.

00:20:39.973 --> 00:20:41.077
- She's just--
- With your eye.

00:20:42.731 --> 00:20:44.370
- She's just like me in that she doesn't,

00:20:44.370 --> 00:20:46.230
she's just, she feels
like, I don't want to

00:20:46.230 --> 00:20:47.063
look stupid.

00:20:47.063 --> 00:20:49.214
I don't wanna be embarrassed.

00:20:49.214 --> 00:20:51.114
So we ended up talking, we only talked to

00:20:51.114 --> 00:20:54.760
people, like she saw
Nate Berkus, you know,

00:20:54.760 --> 00:20:57.770
the designer, and she
had a point of connection

00:20:57.770 --> 00:20:59.970
and she had something and
they've been to the same,

00:20:59.970 --> 00:21:01.760
anyway she talked to him for
a second and that was like,

00:21:01.760 --> 00:21:03.227
cool and that worked.

00:21:03.227 --> 00:21:06.110
But we didn't end up actually
having a conversation

00:21:06.110 --> 00:21:07.910
with any of the cast because at some point

00:21:07.910 --> 00:21:08.960
they ended up just hanging out

00:21:08.960 --> 00:21:11.370
with John Legend and Chrissy Teigen and--

00:21:11.370 --> 00:21:12.203
- [Link] Right.

00:21:12.203 --> 00:21:14.138
- Just in this group and it was like,

00:21:14.138 --> 00:21:15.146
it was impenetrable.

00:21:15.146 --> 00:21:17.210
I actually went up to the group, because

00:21:17.210 --> 00:21:20.610
Lance Bass was on the outside of the group

00:21:20.610 --> 00:21:22.728
and I told Jessie, I was like, I bet that

00:21:22.728 --> 00:21:26.167
Lance Bass knows who I am.

