00:57:54.940 --> 00:57:58.122
- Of course, I kind of need to be invited.

00:57:58.122 --> 00:58:01.496
- Again, I'm grateful, I'm grateful

00:58:01.496 --> 00:58:03.505
that you took the initiative.

00:58:03.505 --> 00:58:06.329
I'm grateful that we have these stories.

00:58:06.329 --> 00:58:08.230
These stories are probably,

00:58:08.230 --> 00:58:10.715
in one sentence, more strategic

00:58:10.715 --> 00:58:14.410
and of more value than the relationship

00:58:14.410 --> 00:58:15.900
that we could have had with those people,

00:58:15.900 --> 00:58:18.130
that we will never have
with those people now.

00:58:18.130 --> 00:58:19.247
But you know what?

00:58:19.247 --> 00:58:23.750
We may, Alex Honnold might
be on the show at some point.

00:58:23.750 --> 00:58:25.410
- Don't forget, we talked to Terry Crews.

00:58:25.410 --> 00:58:26.820
He knew who we are, and he gave us

00:58:26.820 --> 00:58:28.760
a motivational speech that same night.

00:58:28.760 --> 00:58:31.060
- And let me say, I initiated

00:58:31.060 --> 00:58:32.729
the conversation with Terry Crews.

00:58:32.729 --> 00:58:34.116
- That's 'cause we had seen

00:58:34.116 --> 00:58:34.949
him the night before.

00:58:34.949 --> 00:58:36.230
- That's what I'm saying.

00:58:36.230 --> 00:58:37.063
I'm outlining the differences.

00:58:37.063 --> 00:58:39.855
And I'm not saying, I think
that in the setting, you--

00:58:39.855 --> 00:58:41.064
- I talked to Terry.

00:58:41.064 --> 00:58:42.780
- You're better at these things.

00:58:42.780 --> 00:58:45.130
So, what I'm saying is, I will talk

00:58:45.130 --> 00:58:49.030
to anybody if I got a point of contact.

00:58:49.030 --> 00:58:51.228
And so, we had seen him at the,

00:58:51.228 --> 00:58:53.170
he's, by the way, we talked about

00:58:53.170 --> 00:58:55.620
this before, nicest guy on the planet.

00:58:55.620 --> 00:58:57.430
Terry Crews, nicest guy on the planet.

00:58:57.430 --> 00:59:00.770
And actually, he and
his son watch the show,

00:59:00.770 --> 00:59:01.670
it was incredible.

00:59:02.600 --> 00:59:04.641
But we took these rules,

00:59:04.641 --> 00:59:06.030
and we said, the next time we go

00:59:06.030 --> 00:59:08.950
to a party, we're going to apply

00:59:08.950 --> 00:59:10.510
some of these rules.

00:59:10.510 --> 00:59:14.470
And so, we got invited to the...

00:59:16.589 --> 00:59:19.943
HBO Golden Globes after party.

00:59:21.884 --> 00:59:23.380
And I was coming back from,

00:59:23.380 --> 00:59:25.672
first of all, it was, you know,

00:59:25.672 --> 00:59:27.677
we were told, I think you probably could,

00:59:27.677 --> 00:59:29.200
you didn't have to have a tux,

00:59:29.200 --> 00:59:31.630
but technically black tie.

00:59:31.630 --> 00:59:33.430
We didn't have tuxes.

00:59:33.430 --> 00:59:35.950
I was in Mexico at the time,

00:59:35.950 --> 00:59:38.770
and I was gonna have to get back,

00:59:38.770 --> 00:59:41.150
get fitted for a tux,
because the Rhettster

00:59:41.150 --> 00:59:42.470
don't wear something off the rack

00:59:42.470 --> 00:59:44.435
because they don't make
things that fit me, okay?

00:59:44.435 --> 00:59:46.350
So, I have to get things fitted,

00:59:46.350 --> 00:59:48.547
I have to get things tailored

00:59:48.547 --> 00:59:50.216
if they're gonna look halfway decent.

00:59:50.216 --> 00:59:52.580
So, I was gonna have to get off the plane,

00:59:52.580 --> 00:59:54.000
come here to the office, get fitted

00:59:54.000 --> 00:59:56.270
for a tux, and them immediately

00:59:56.270 --> 00:59:57.740
get into a car and go to this party,

00:59:57.740 --> 00:59:59.530
which is what happened.

00:59:59.530 --> 01:00:02.033
And I was actually a little bit late

01:00:02.033 --> 01:00:03.040
because there was a flight delay.

01:00:03.040 --> 01:00:05.980
So, we're going down, and apparently all

01:00:05.980 --> 01:00:07.750
the parties after the Golden Globes

01:00:07.750 --> 01:00:09.590
are at the hotel, the Beverley Hilton

01:00:09.590 --> 01:00:11.390
where the Golden Globes are held.

01:00:11.390 --> 01:00:13.330
And they're all in these little areas,

01:00:13.330 --> 01:00:15.064
so you got Netflix and Amazon and Hulu

01:00:15.064 --> 01:00:17.150
or whatever, and HBO.

01:00:17.150 --> 01:00:19.790
So, there's like six parties.

01:00:19.790 --> 01:00:21.917
Like, big, significant parties,

01:00:21.917 --> 01:00:23.680
and they're all in the same place,

01:00:23.680 --> 01:00:24.930
and so, because the traffic would be

01:00:24.930 --> 01:00:26.270
so crazy to this little hotel,

01:00:26.270 --> 01:00:28.850
they have a shuttle service where you

01:00:28.850 --> 01:00:31.260
meet offsite at a parking area,

01:00:31.260 --> 01:00:32.670
and you get into these shuttles.

01:00:32.670 --> 01:00:34.320
- And we were told to Uber to

01:00:34.320 --> 01:00:36.480
the location of the
shuttles, then a shuttle

01:00:36.480 --> 01:00:37.830
will take you to the party,

01:00:37.830 --> 01:00:39.590
and then, you know, bring your ID

01:00:39.590 --> 01:00:41.655
so you can, you know.

01:00:41.655 --> 01:00:42.840
- Because there's a list.

01:00:42.840 --> 01:00:43.700
- There's a list.

01:00:43.700 --> 01:00:44.533
- Right.

01:00:45.400 --> 01:00:47.760
So, we get to the shuttle area, and we see

01:00:47.760 --> 01:00:49.710
just a bunch of shuttles lined up,

01:00:49.710 --> 01:00:50.810
and we go to the first one,

01:00:50.810 --> 01:00:53.170
and it's closed, and it's full.

01:00:53.170 --> 01:00:54.750
We go to the second one, it's closed,

01:00:54.750 --> 01:00:55.583
and it's full.

01:00:55.583 --> 01:00:57.848
We go to the third one, the door's open.

01:00:57.848 --> 01:00:59.200
What do we do?

01:00:59.200 --> 01:01:00.430
We go on the shuttle.

01:01:00.430 --> 01:01:01.880
- Yeah, I go up in the shuttle.

01:01:01.880 --> 01:01:03.260
And lo and behold, the shuttle's full

01:01:03.260 --> 01:01:05.180
except for two seats.

01:01:05.180 --> 01:01:06.288
(angelic singing)

01:01:06.288 --> 01:01:07.370
- How many of us are there?

01:01:07.370 --> 01:01:08.203
- Two.

01:01:08.203 --> 01:01:09.761
Perfect math.

01:01:09.761 --> 01:01:10.927
- Just the two of us.

01:01:10.927 --> 01:01:11.880
- So we sat down.

01:01:11.880 --> 01:01:13.470
- We sit down, and then we begin

01:01:13.470 --> 01:01:14.920
to have a conversation with a woman

01:01:14.920 --> 01:01:16.828
who's sitting next to us.

01:01:16.828 --> 01:01:19.660
And this conversation concerns

01:01:19.660 --> 01:01:20.730
me a little bit, you know,

01:01:20.730 --> 01:01:21.940
as the one who tends to worry

01:01:21.940 --> 01:01:23.210
a little bit more and try to figure

01:01:23.210 --> 01:01:24.043
out if we're doing the right thing.

01:01:24.043 --> 01:01:25.500
- Yeah, I was feeling great.

01:01:25.500 --> 01:01:27.110
- You were just like,
we're on the shuttle,

01:01:27.110 --> 01:01:28.230
we're on the shuttle, it's great.

01:01:28.230 --> 01:01:29.480
- And I was like, but something doesn't

01:01:29.480 --> 01:01:31.650
seem right about this, because we didn't

01:01:31.650 --> 01:01:33.771
talk to anybody, we
just got on the shuttle,

01:01:33.771 --> 01:01:36.890
and then we talked, and the woman

01:01:36.890 --> 01:01:38.948
was not going to the HBO party.

01:01:38.948 --> 01:01:41.763
I think she was already under

01:01:41.763 --> 01:01:43.960
the influence of something.

01:01:43.960 --> 01:01:45.130
- Okay.

01:01:45.130 --> 01:01:46.400
- There was something going on there

01:01:46.400 --> 01:01:48.962
because it was not clear
communication from her.

01:01:48.962 --> 01:01:52.444
I didn't want to seem uncool, but I was

01:01:52.444 --> 01:01:55.890
just like, is this going to the HBO party?

01:01:55.890 --> 01:01:58.800
And she was like, "well, it
goes to all the parties."

01:01:58.800 --> 01:02:00.521
And then I'm like, "what do you mean?

01:02:00.521 --> 01:02:02.250
"Are we gonna be dropped
off at different parties?"

01:02:02.250 --> 01:02:03.607
We didn't know that all the parties

01:02:03.607 --> 01:02:04.440
were at the same place.

01:02:04.440 --> 01:02:05.537
We knew nothing.

01:02:05.537 --> 01:02:07.260
I'm beginning to think we should

01:02:07.260 --> 01:02:09.504
get off of the shuttle and tell people,

01:02:09.504 --> 01:02:12.840
hey, we want to go to the HBO party.

01:02:12.840 --> 01:02:14.380
- We don't belong here is what

01:02:14.380 --> 01:02:15.650
it sounded like to me, so I'm like,

01:02:15.650 --> 01:02:17.950
nope, staying put on the shuttle.

01:02:17.950 --> 01:02:19.290
I'm not gonna admit defeat in front

01:02:19.290 --> 01:02:21.150
of everybody on this shuttle

01:02:21.150 --> 01:02:22.670
by having a walk of shame.

01:02:22.670 --> 01:02:24.650
- Stay tuned to what actually happened.

01:02:24.650 --> 01:02:25.483
- Walk of shame.

01:02:25.483 --> 01:02:27.650
And then the shuttle starts
moving, so we don't--

01:02:27.650 --> 01:02:28.825
- Too late at that point.

01:02:28.825 --> 01:02:29.658
- We're, like, arguing with each other

01:02:29.658 --> 01:02:32.600
under our breath, and I'm
trying to calm Rhett down.

01:02:32.600 --> 01:02:34.797
And then it's like, well,
the shuttle's moving.

01:02:34.797 --> 01:02:35.960
There's nothing we can do now.

01:02:35.960 --> 01:02:37.820
We finally get over there
to the Beverley Hilton--

01:02:37.820 --> 01:02:39.260
- Which was like, half a mile away,

01:02:39.260 --> 01:02:40.160
it wasn't even that far.

01:02:40.160 --> 01:02:42.840
- They let us off, and then they're like,

01:02:42.840 --> 01:02:46.256
a lot of security people
on the red carpet there,

01:02:46.256 --> 01:02:48.258
and they're like wrist bands, wrist bands.

01:02:48.258 --> 01:02:49.560
And I'm like, wrist bands?

01:02:49.560 --> 01:02:51.950
I ain't heard nothing
about no wrist bands.

01:02:51.950 --> 01:02:54.640
- And everyone on the
shuttle has a wrist band

01:02:54.640 --> 01:02:56.323
except you know who, the two guys

01:02:56.323 --> 01:02:58.020
that just walked onto the shuttle

01:02:58.020 --> 01:03:00.530
randomly, because
apparently there was a whole

01:03:00.530 --> 01:03:03.200
thing at the parking place where you had

01:03:03.200 --> 01:03:05.394
to get checked in and get your wrist

01:03:05.394 --> 01:03:07.273
band so you could get into the hotel.

01:03:08.230 --> 01:03:09.966
- There were no signs,
there was no orientation.

01:03:09.966 --> 01:03:11.572
- Yeah, in our defense,
no one told us this.

01:03:11.572 --> 01:03:13.290
- And there was other
people who were like,

01:03:13.290 --> 01:03:15.003
oh, we Ubered directly here

01:03:15.003 --> 01:03:16.930
because I didn't want
to get on that shuttle,

01:03:16.930 --> 01:03:19.410
and I don't have a wrist band either,

01:03:19.410 --> 01:03:21.430
so this woman's, like, taking down names

01:03:21.430 --> 01:03:24.620
and going, she's with HBO and she's

01:03:24.620 --> 01:03:26.924
going to get wrist bands.

01:03:26.924 --> 01:03:30.240
- Okay, now, at this point, talk about

01:03:30.240 --> 01:03:31.590
being a little bit embarrassed,

01:03:31.590 --> 01:03:33.601
if you're talking about
trying to save face

01:03:33.601 --> 01:03:36.087
for the shuttle, what
ended up happening is,

01:03:36.087 --> 01:03:37.670
everyone's getting off these shuttles

01:03:37.670 --> 01:03:40.010
and just walking straight past security,

01:03:40.010 --> 01:03:43.625
and you and I and some real estate people,

01:03:43.625 --> 01:03:46.410
they said that they were real estate,

01:03:46.410 --> 01:03:48.536
are all standing out there.

01:03:48.536 --> 01:03:50.520
- Like fans.

01:03:50.520 --> 01:03:51.353
- Yeah.

01:03:51.353 --> 01:03:52.843
Not able to get in.

01:03:52.843 --> 01:03:54.666
And we look like two
guys that just dressed

01:03:54.666 --> 01:03:56.020
up and walked, and we're
just hoping we could

01:03:56.020 --> 01:03:57.755
slide by security like the Grammy video

01:03:57.755 --> 01:03:58.793
we did years ago.

01:03:58.793 --> 01:04:00.560
- Because that does happen.

01:04:00.560 --> 01:04:02.160
There are people lurking and trying

01:04:02.160 --> 01:04:04.863
to look like they belong, and just get in.

01:04:04.863 --> 01:04:06.120
Jeff Bridges was leaving.

01:04:06.120 --> 01:04:07.610
- All kinds of people
were coming and going.

01:04:07.610 --> 01:04:10.140
All kinds of very recognizable actors.

01:04:10.140 --> 01:04:11.897
- My favorite actor--

01:04:11.897 --> 01:04:14.450
- Stephen Root walked behind you.

01:04:14.450 --> 01:04:15.517
- I know.

01:04:15.517 --> 01:04:16.860
And then you didn't tell me until

01:04:16.860 --> 01:04:17.986
he was already gone.

01:04:17.986 --> 01:04:19.410
- Because I didn't want
you, and you should

01:04:19.410 --> 01:04:20.443
thank me for this.

01:04:21.302 --> 01:04:23.230
I didn't want you to meet your favorite

01:04:23.230 --> 01:04:25.270
character actor, Stephen Root--

01:04:25.270 --> 01:04:27.150
- On the outside of a party where it--

01:04:27.150 --> 01:04:28.096
- Without a wrist band.

01:04:28.096 --> 01:04:29.097
- Yeah.

01:04:29.097 --> 01:04:30.950
- You didn't want to do that either.

01:04:30.950 --> 01:04:31.783
- Nope.

01:04:31.783 --> 01:04:33.361
- So, thank me.

01:04:33.361 --> 01:04:35.950
- I'm not ready to do
that, because he wasn't

01:04:35.950 --> 01:04:37.250
in the party, Rhett.

01:04:37.250 --> 01:04:38.240
He wasn't in our party.

01:04:38.240 --> 01:04:40.479
- Yeah, but he would have
been like, you coming?

01:04:40.479 --> 01:04:41.692
And you would have been like,

01:04:41.692 --> 01:04:42.872
as soon as I get a wrist band.

01:04:42.872 --> 01:04:43.905
And he would have been like, oh,

01:04:43.905 --> 01:04:44.950
he's one of those guys.

01:04:44.950 --> 01:04:47.540
But we may have ended up fairing better

01:04:47.540 --> 01:04:49.270
than if we hadn't gotten on the shuttle.

01:04:49.270 --> 01:04:50.425
- I think we did.

01:04:50.425 --> 01:04:54.403
- Because it did take about 30 minutes of,

01:04:55.718 --> 01:04:59.666
I was kind of frantically our PR people,

01:04:59.666 --> 01:05:01.770
because I thought that we were not gonna

01:05:01.770 --> 01:05:03.742
get in at that point, we were

01:05:03.742 --> 01:05:04.947
gonna have to go back to home base and it

01:05:04.947 --> 01:05:06.000
was gonna set us back forever.

01:05:06.000 --> 01:05:07.860
But eventually, we did get,

01:05:07.860 --> 01:05:09.960
somebody came out and gave us wrist bands,

01:05:09.960 --> 01:05:11.419
and then we were able to check in.

01:05:11.419 --> 01:05:13.540
It did take about 30
minutes, and a lot of people

01:05:13.540 --> 01:05:14.600
walking by.

01:05:14.600 --> 01:05:16.220
But we have reason to believe that if

01:05:16.220 --> 01:05:17.530
we had have gone all the way to the

01:05:17.530 --> 01:05:19.670
back of the line and
checked in the right way,

01:05:19.670 --> 01:05:20.503
we probably would have gotten

01:05:20.503 --> 01:05:22.980
to the party like an
hour and a half later.

01:05:22.980 --> 01:05:26.188
It was ridiculous how late this thing was.

01:05:26.188 --> 01:05:27.480
But then we go in.

01:05:27.480 --> 01:05:29.300
- So, we got in earlier.

01:05:29.300 --> 01:05:33.240
- But we got in, and, uh,

01:05:33.240 --> 01:05:35.010
this party was different.

01:05:35.010 --> 01:05:36.440
It was bigger.

01:05:36.440 --> 01:05:38.470
- You could get plates
full of food at this party,

01:05:38.470 --> 01:05:40.490
and there were seats.

01:05:40.490 --> 01:05:44.090
There were tables, like round tables.

01:05:44.090 --> 01:05:45.260
It was much more laid back.

01:05:45.260 --> 01:05:46.880
It was more like a dinner party.

01:05:46.880 --> 01:05:48.970
Well, not a dinner party, but a party

01:05:48.970 --> 01:05:50.320
where you could eat dinner.

01:05:51.518 --> 01:05:53.007
(Link laughing)

01:05:53.007 --> 01:05:54.420
- Yeah, a party where you can eat dinner.

01:05:54.420 --> 01:05:55.850
- But not a dinner party where everybody's

01:05:55.850 --> 01:05:57.450
seated and someone gives a speech,

01:05:57.450 --> 01:05:58.977
that's not it.

01:05:58.977 --> 01:05:59.970
- But I would say the percentage of--

01:05:59.970 --> 01:06:01.590
- Really famous people was--

01:06:01.590 --> 01:06:03.880
- Lower percentage of
really famous people,

01:06:03.880 --> 01:06:06.270
but a lot of, like, I know that guy

01:06:06.270 --> 01:06:07.410
from that movie, I know that guy

01:06:07.410 --> 01:06:08.910
from that show, but I don't know his name,

01:06:08.910 --> 01:06:09.780
and you probably wouldn't either,

01:06:09.780 --> 01:06:11.402
but you'd recognize him.

01:06:11.402 --> 01:06:12.720
It was a lot of those people and then

01:06:12.720 --> 01:06:13.810
a lot of industry people.

01:06:13.810 --> 01:06:16.422
And it was a much larger party

01:06:16.422 --> 01:06:18.940
in terms of space and
in terms of attendance.

01:06:18.940 --> 01:06:20.750
- We had some good
conversations with people who,

01:06:20.750 --> 01:06:22.190
you know, again, it's good to have

01:06:22.190 --> 01:06:24.490
industry conversations, meet producers

01:06:24.490 --> 01:06:25.650
and all this type of stuff.

01:06:25.650 --> 01:06:29.090
So, it's like, and a number of those

01:06:29.090 --> 01:06:29.940
people talked to us because

01:06:29.940 --> 01:06:31.660
they knew who we were.

01:06:31.660 --> 01:06:34.920
Sometimes because their
kids know who we were,

01:06:34.920 --> 01:06:36.240
but hey, that's a good in.

01:06:36.240 --> 01:06:38.160
I'll take it any way I can get it.

01:06:38.160 --> 01:06:41.319
And we also, well, we had a couple

01:06:41.319 --> 01:06:43.770
people that we wanted to talk to, right?

01:06:43.770 --> 01:06:47.005
It's a HBO party, so we thought that

01:06:47.005 --> 01:06:49.430
Mark and Jay Duplass
would be there, right?

01:06:49.430 --> 01:06:51.330
We both finished reading their book.

01:06:51.330 --> 01:06:52.420
- Yup.

01:06:52.420 --> 01:06:53.700
- Fans of theirs.

01:06:53.700 --> 01:06:54.533
We think--

01:06:54.533 --> 01:06:56.535
- I'd like to have a
conversation with them.

01:06:56.535 --> 01:06:57.368
- We'd like to talk to those guys.

01:06:57.368 --> 01:06:58.330
Because we just think that--

01:06:58.330 --> 01:07:00.750
- Just relate to their relationship.

01:07:00.750 --> 01:07:04.517
- Similar backgrounds
and similar philosophies,

01:07:04.517 --> 01:07:06.603
but they weren't there.

01:07:06.603 --> 01:07:09.680
They could have been there,
and maybe we missed them,

01:07:09.680 --> 01:07:10.950
but we didn't see them.

01:07:10.950 --> 01:07:12.964
Because I was trying
to, and maybe I pushed

01:07:12.964 --> 01:07:16.060
it too far in my direction, which,

01:07:16.060 --> 01:07:17.850
I was like, let's talk to people

01:07:17.850 --> 01:07:20.020
that we've got a reason to talk to.

01:07:20.020 --> 01:07:22.010
That doesn't mean we have to know them,

01:07:22.010 --> 01:07:23.750
but, like, let's initiate a conversation

01:07:23.750 --> 01:07:24.790
and there's, like, an in.

01:07:24.790 --> 01:07:26.040
With those guys, it would have been like,

01:07:26.040 --> 01:07:28.060
hey, we just read your book.

01:07:28.060 --> 01:07:29.060
And first of all, that
would mean something

01:07:29.060 --> 01:07:31.240
to them because we're not talking

01:07:31.240 --> 01:07:33.680
about Room 104 or whatever everybody

01:07:33.680 --> 01:07:34.513
else is talking about.

01:07:34.513 --> 01:07:36.240
We're talking about
this thing that, like--

01:07:36.240 --> 01:07:37.073
- Pet project.

01:07:37.073 --> 01:07:38.040
- You guys like the book?

01:07:38.040 --> 01:07:39.160
Yeah, we just listened to it,

01:07:39.160 --> 01:07:40.330
here's all these parallels

01:07:40.330 --> 01:07:42.550
that are really interesting
between us and you guys.

01:07:42.550 --> 01:07:43.850
- You were prepped for that.

01:07:43.850 --> 01:07:45.983
- I was ready for that conversation.

01:07:45.983 --> 01:07:48.064
But that didn't happen.

01:07:48.064 --> 01:07:50.954
We saw Pete Holmes, who had been

01:07:50.954 --> 01:07:53.690
on Good Mythical Morning.

01:07:53.690 --> 01:07:55.436
- Let's call him a friend of the show.

01:07:55.436 --> 01:07:56.269
- Friend of the show.

01:07:56.269 --> 01:07:57.960
And had a conversation, met his wife

01:07:57.960 --> 01:07:59.710
for the first time, had
a great conversation

01:07:59.710 --> 01:08:00.543
with Pete.

01:08:00.543 --> 01:08:03.323
He actually said basically the same thing,

01:08:03.323 --> 01:08:04.156
he was like, "it took us forever

01:08:04.156 --> 01:08:06.277
"to get into this party,
and I'm glad I ran

01:08:06.277 --> 01:08:09.117
"into you guys, because
having a conversation

01:08:09.117 --> 01:08:11.350
"I want to be in makes it worth it."

01:08:11.350 --> 01:08:12.710
That felt great.

01:08:12.710 --> 01:08:14.479
You know, 'cause he's
thinking the same thing.

01:08:14.479 --> 01:08:16.900
He's got a show on HBO and he's thinking

01:08:16.900 --> 01:08:17.733
the same thing.

01:08:17.733 --> 01:08:19.050
Like, who am I gonna
talk to at this thing.

01:08:19.050 --> 01:08:21.200
- But let's not make it out to be like,

01:08:21.200 --> 01:08:22.990
we have to have certain
types of interactions

01:08:22.990 --> 01:08:24.700
at a party to feel good about ourselves.

01:08:24.700 --> 01:08:25.790
Because earlier, you established

01:08:25.790 --> 01:08:27.060
that we don't need that.

01:08:27.060 --> 01:08:28.830
- Well, but I'm not the one that tries to,

01:08:28.830 --> 01:08:30.690
well, then what is your goal in all

01:08:30.690 --> 01:08:32.460
the conversations that
you try to initiate?

01:08:32.460 --> 01:08:33.800
You're just trying to have a good time?

01:08:33.800 --> 01:08:34.750
- Move and shake.

01:08:34.750 --> 01:08:36.460
I mean, there is a business to this,

01:08:36.460 --> 01:08:39.240
but it's not, it's what, I don't need

01:08:39.240 --> 01:08:41.120
to feel good about myself.

01:08:41.120 --> 01:08:42.410
And I don't think you do either,

01:08:42.410 --> 01:08:43.830
but I'm just saying that it sounded

01:08:43.830 --> 01:08:45.170
like it in that moment where it's like,

01:08:45.170 --> 01:08:46.620
oh, it felt good for somebody to say

01:08:46.620 --> 01:08:47.570
they wanted to talk to us.

01:08:47.570 --> 01:08:49.250
And it did feel good.

01:08:49.250 --> 01:08:52.010
But it's just a weird, it's a weird

01:08:52.010 --> 01:08:53.912
environment where, like, and maybe

01:08:53.912 --> 01:08:57.923
this is kind of true of LA in general,

01:08:57.923 --> 01:09:01.246
is that it's people trying to

01:09:01.246 --> 01:09:05.680
get themselves noticed or get their

01:09:05.680 --> 01:09:07.010
project accomplished.

01:09:07.010 --> 01:09:10.010
Or to make their way.

01:09:10.010 --> 01:09:14.119
And so, it's, you know, industry parties

01:09:14.119 --> 01:09:15.970
are industry parties.

01:09:15.970 --> 01:09:18.285
They're to work.

01:09:18.285 --> 01:09:20.560
You know, it's not like a friend party,

01:09:20.560 --> 01:09:22.030
like you said, where, like,

01:09:22.030 --> 01:09:24.440
yeah, there may be a bunch of celebrities

01:09:24.440 --> 01:09:27.216
at a party, and boy,
wouldn't that be interesting,

01:09:27.216 --> 01:09:30.940
but they're there because they're friends.

01:09:30.940 --> 01:09:32.580
That's' not an industry party.

01:09:32.580 --> 01:09:34.375
- Well, because, I mean--

01:09:34.375 --> 01:09:35.790
- Gotta get something done.

01:09:35.790 --> 01:09:37.972
- Well, because one of the things

01:09:37.972 --> 01:09:39.280
that we're thinking about,

01:09:39.280 --> 01:09:40.830
just strategically, creatively,

01:09:42.849 --> 01:09:45.250
I don't know, one of the
things that we've learned

01:09:46.922 --> 01:09:48.130
is getting really qualified people

01:09:48.130 --> 01:09:50.879
to help you make things happen

01:09:50.879 --> 01:09:54.190
is, that's what we want to do, right?

01:09:54.190 --> 01:09:56.010
I mean, that's the reason that we're doing

01:09:56.010 --> 01:09:58.620
what we do today, is
because at some point,

01:09:58.620 --> 01:10:00.940
we figured out, oh, you
know what really works?

01:10:00.940 --> 01:10:02.590
Is getting people who can do things better

01:10:02.590 --> 01:10:04.750
than we can to do those things.

01:10:04.750 --> 01:10:06.080
And that's why we have a team now.

01:10:06.080 --> 01:10:08.090
But the same thing applies to,

01:10:08.090 --> 01:10:09.891
who are you gonna work with?

01:10:09.891 --> 01:10:10.724
Who are you gonna collaborate with

01:10:10.724 --> 01:10:11.557
on this project?

01:10:11.557 --> 01:10:14.140
Who's gonna help write it, produce it,

01:10:14.140 --> 01:10:15.080
who's gonna act in it?

01:10:15.080 --> 01:10:17.012
That kind of thing, and things

01:10:17.012 --> 01:10:18.046
that we want to do.

01:10:18.046 --> 01:10:19.060
And so, you want to have those connections

01:10:19.060 --> 01:10:21.420
so that, when you say, here's the idea,

01:10:21.420 --> 01:10:23.010
will you help make it happen?

01:10:23.010 --> 01:10:25.010
Would you like to be in it, to an actor

01:10:25.010 --> 01:10:27.360
or whatever, it's like, oh, yeah,

01:10:27.360 --> 01:10:29.372
I do, because either I saw you

01:10:29.372 --> 01:10:30.930
at that party and I saw you guys

01:10:30.930 --> 01:10:32.370
on the red carpet, and then I looked,

01:10:32.370 --> 01:10:35.040
you know, these little touch points matter

01:10:35.040 --> 01:10:36.670
if you want to play that game.

01:10:36.670 --> 01:10:38.140
- But it's all unspoken.

01:10:38.140 --> 01:10:40.420
I don't think, well,
maybe there is a booklet

01:10:40.420 --> 01:10:43.140
or something, but, and
maybe I could have saved

01:10:43.140 --> 01:10:45.700
a lot of heartache, and sidestepped

01:10:45.700 --> 01:10:48.810
a fun podcast though, by reading it.

01:10:48.810 --> 01:10:51.280
- I don't think that any
damage has been done.

01:10:51.280 --> 01:10:52.113
- No.

01:10:52.113 --> 01:10:53.340
- Let me just clarify that--

01:10:53.340 --> 01:10:54.660
- I didn't say it had been.

01:10:54.660 --> 01:10:58.114
- I think that even the most

01:10:58.114 --> 01:11:01.433
embarrassing interaction that you had

01:11:01.433 --> 01:11:04.677
with Mr. David Burd, Lil Dicky,

01:11:04.677 --> 01:11:06.190
is what they call him.

01:11:06.190 --> 01:11:07.263
He has a rap name.

01:11:08.437 --> 01:11:09.950
- I call him Dave.

01:11:09.950 --> 01:11:13.303
- Even that conversation, the chances

01:11:13.303 --> 01:11:16.289
of us working with Lil Dicky

01:11:16.289 --> 01:11:20.329
actually went up because
of the interaction.

01:11:20.329 --> 01:11:23.650
Now, there are interactions where

01:11:23.650 --> 01:11:25.430
the chances would have gone down, right?

01:11:25.430 --> 01:11:27.790
The chances would have gone down,

01:11:27.790 --> 01:11:32.209
they were at a tipping,
they were right there

01:11:32.209 --> 01:11:35.657
in a real gray area for a second there.

01:11:35.657 --> 01:11:39.463
- Glad I didn't have a
rock with John Mayer.

01:11:39.463 --> 01:11:41.466
That would have been horrible.

01:11:41.466 --> 01:11:43.000
- But I do think that
the most important thing

01:11:43.000 --> 01:11:44.833
is just beginning the conversation,

01:11:45.840 --> 01:11:49.600
but I do think that we now know

01:11:49.600 --> 01:11:52.332
how to be a tad more strategic.

01:11:52.332 --> 01:11:54.650
- I think that there were no mishaps

01:11:54.650 --> 01:11:56.909
at the Golden Globe party,

01:11:56.909 --> 01:11:58.426
except for the shuttle thing,

01:11:58.426 --> 01:12:00.431
which I think ended up being great.

01:12:00.431 --> 01:12:01.264
We got there early.

01:12:01.264 --> 01:12:04.160
So, I don't think I have any demerits.

01:12:04.160 --> 01:12:06.940
- No, lessons learned at Golden Globes.

01:12:06.940 --> 01:12:08.994
- At the HBO party.

01:12:08.994 --> 01:12:10.400
- Yeah, I can't think of any

01:12:10.400 --> 01:12:11.806
lessons learned at the
Golden Globes party.

01:12:11.806 --> 01:12:13.310
- And I got a tux out of it.

01:12:13.310 --> 01:12:15.490
Well, I mean, I bought it.

01:12:15.490 --> 01:12:16.950
- Well, I'll tell you
one lesson we learned,

01:12:16.950 --> 01:12:18.435
we actually applied it.

01:12:18.435 --> 01:12:20.230
After you go through the red carpet

01:12:20.230 --> 01:12:21.970
and get your pictures
taken by the professional

01:12:21.970 --> 01:12:24.390
photographers, you go
back to the red carpet

01:12:24.390 --> 01:12:26.010
at the end of the night,
and there will be people

01:12:26.010 --> 01:12:28.330
taking their picture with their iPhones.

01:12:28.330 --> 01:12:30.130
You get one of them to take a picture

01:12:30.130 --> 01:12:33.043
of you with your phone, and

01:12:33.043 --> 01:12:36.869
that will allow you to have a picture on

01:12:36.869 --> 01:12:39.691
your camera roll that isn't,

01:12:39.691 --> 01:12:42.230
you don't have to wait until

01:12:42.230 --> 01:12:44.745
the next day to get some Getty image

01:12:44.745 --> 01:12:46.240
or something like that.

01:12:46.240 --> 01:12:47.281
- That's right.

01:12:47.281 --> 01:12:49.298
- So, the picture that we posted

01:12:49.298 --> 01:12:50.131
was just a picture from the phone.

01:12:51.310 --> 01:12:52.513
That's a little hack.

01:12:53.360 --> 01:12:54.800
That's a little insider tip.

01:12:54.800 --> 01:12:56.451
- There it is.

01:12:56.451 --> 01:12:58.592
So, we're gonna, so, now,

01:12:58.592 --> 01:13:00.980
next time we post photos

01:13:00.980 --> 01:13:02.630
from the next thing we go to,

01:13:02.630 --> 01:13:05.210
you're gonna be thinking, man,

01:13:05.210 --> 01:13:08.460
that's a lot more complicated
than I thought it was.

01:13:08.460 --> 01:13:10.365
Lots of ins and outs.

01:13:10.365 --> 01:13:11.610
- Yeah.

01:13:11.610 --> 01:13:14.150
- So, thanks for hanging out with us.

01:13:14.150 --> 01:13:16.530
Thanks for learning along with us.

01:13:16.530 --> 01:13:17.840
Because, I mean, let's be clear.

01:13:17.840 --> 01:13:20.969
We both learned a lot, right?

01:13:20.969 --> 01:13:23.282
- I learned so much watching you.

01:13:23.282 --> 01:13:24.210
(Link laughing)

01:13:24.210 --> 01:13:25.270
So much.

01:13:25.270 --> 01:13:26.480
- Yeah, I'm a...

01:13:28.240 --> 01:13:30.853
I'm a teacher, man, I'm
a teacher in action.

01:13:31.870 --> 01:13:33.299
What not to do.

01:13:33.299 --> 01:13:34.663
- Yeah, you teach by example.

01:13:36.270 --> 01:13:38.270
You teach by bad examples.

01:13:38.270 --> 01:13:39.634
(Link laughing)

01:13:39.634 --> 01:13:41.380
It is a form of teaching.

01:13:41.380 --> 01:13:42.430
I admit it.

01:13:42.430 --> 01:13:43.263
It is fun.

01:13:43.263 --> 01:13:46.170
I'm enjoying myself, and Stephen Root,

01:13:46.170 --> 01:13:47.440
I'm coming for you.

